# Derived index artifacts are written by generators that always emit LF.
# Without this, git's autocrlf would rewrite the working copy to CRLF on
# Windows and the generator's next run would show a spurious diff.
#
# One generator writes a pinned index that git tracks:
#   tools/diagrams/archify-artifacts.mjs   -> **/_archify/index.json
#
# It was missing from this list once, and fourteen index files reported as
# modified after every re-render while git diff showed nothing.
#
# `**/_meta/*.json` used to be pinned beside it, for the predecessor generator's
# staleness check. Local ADR 0004 took the derived knowledge layer out of version
# control entirely, and local ADR 0015 moved the database into the app's storage,
# so no tracked file is left for that rule to apply to.
#
# Only the generated index is pinned. The Archify specifications beside it are
# authored by hand, and pinning those would change what a Windows editor writes
# instead of fixing a generator's phantom diff. The same goes for each knowledge
# folder's authored `_reading-order.json`, which no generator writes.
**/_archify/index.json text eol=lf

# Test fixtures are byte-exact inputs: a PDF's xref offsets and a JPEG's EXIF
# would break under line-ending conversion.
tests/**/Fixtures/** binary
